---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
const matomo = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_MATOMO_SITE_ID);
---

<LegalPage title="Cookie policy" description="Which cookies the Incoltec website uses and how to manage them." heading="Cookie policy" updated="Last updated: November 2026">
  <h2>1. What cookies are</h2>
  <p>Cookies and similar technologies are small files the site stores on your device to make it work or to learn how it is used.</p>

  <h2>2. Cookies we use</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Cookie</th><th>Owner</th><th>Type</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>cc_cookie</td><td>Incoltec (first party)</td><td>Technical, necessary</td><td>Remembers your cookie preferences</td><td>6 months</td></tr>
      {matomo && <tr><td>_pk_id.*</td><td>Incoltec (Matomo, self-hosted)</td><td>Analytics</td><td>Distinguishes visitors pseudonymously</td><td>13 months</td></tr>}
      {matomo && <tr><td>_pk_ses.*</td><td>Incoltec (Matomo, self-hosted)</td><td>Analytics</td><td>Groups the pages of one visit</td><td>30 minutes</td></tr>}
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Analytics cookies are only set if you accept them. {!matomo && 'The site currently uses no analytics or advertising cookies.'}</p>
  <p>The map on the contact page (OpenStreetMap) and links to Google Maps, LinkedIn or YouTube only load third-party content when you click them; from then on those services' policies apply.</p>

  <h2>3. How to manage or withdraw consent</h2>
  <p>You can change your preferences at any time:</p>
  <p><button type="button" class="cc-btn" data-cc="show-preferencesModal">Cookie settings</button></p>
  <p>You can also delete or block cookies in your browser settings.</p>
</LegalPage>
